# tools/setup/manifests/one-liner-tools — the one-liner installer REGISTRY (operator 2026-05-31):
# declarative entries for tools/CLIs that DON'T come from a package manager and ship their own
# one-line installer (curl|bash etc.). The package-manager CLIs (claude/codex/gemini = bun-global)
# live in manifests/agent-clis; system tools live in manifests/{apt,brew,windows}; runtimes in
# .mise.toml. This file is the escape hatch for everything else, kept declarative like the rest.
#
# Installed by common/one-liner-tools.sh (Unix). DETECT-FIRST (skip if the binary is already on
# PATH — efficient, no re-download; remove the binary + re-run to reinstall/update) + BEST-EFFORT
# (a failed installer WARNS and continues — these are auth-gated peer/dev CLIs, not hard deps;
# LOGIN/auth is the operator's to do after install; never bricks install).
#
# Format per line:  <detect-binary>  <install one-liner (the REST of the line; run via bash -c)>
# `#` comments + blank lines ignored. These are Unix (bash/sh) one-liners; Windows ships separate
# installers (iex/PS) and gets its own registry once the option-B disk work settles.
#
# Pins per dep-pin-search-first (WebSearch 2026-05-31; forge=ForgeCode operator-confirmed 2026-05-31):
#   grok          (Grok Build, xAI)      — https://x.ai/cli
#   cursor-agent  (Cursor CLI)           — https://cursor.com/cli
#   kiro          (Kiro CLI)             — https://kiro.dev/docs/cli/installation
#   hermes        (NousResearch hermes-agent; bundles a local Hindsight memory daemon on first use)
#                 — https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent
#   forge         (ForgeCode — the operator's current forge) — https://forgecode.dev
grok           curl -fsSL https://x.ai/cli/install.sh | bash
cursor-agent   curl https://cursor.com/install -fsSL | bash
kiro           curl -fsSL https://cli.kiro.dev/install | bash
hermes         curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/main/scripts/install.sh | bash
forge          curl -fsSL https://forgecode.dev/cli | sh
